WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.058
A reversed card is one that lands upside
down in your tarot spread.

00:00:05.058 --> 00:00:09.664
You can read it as a twist on the card's
theme, or leave reversals out entirely.

00:00:10.964 --> 00:00:12.134
Upright and reversed.

00:00:12.134 --> 00:00:18.487
A card is upright when it faces you the right way up as you
read it, and reversed when it is turned the other way.

00:00:19.787 --> 00:00:21.684
Three ways to read a reversed card.

00:00:21.684 --> 00:00:25.804
There is no single rule, and different
readers handle reversals differently.

00:00:25.804 --> 00:00:28.785
Here are the three approaches you will
meet most often.

00:00:30.185 --> 00:00:32.536
Have a tarot spread in front of you?

00:00:32.536 --> 00:00:37.302
Photograph it at readmyspread.com, and get
a clear reading, card by card.
